messages.content:
We must rethink the "Project" in solopreneur view. View is intended for managament users that need to review the tasks status. In codx-junior a project represents: a folder with files, profiles, settings and much more (this will remain untouched, just for your info) and then we have sprint boards that manages tasks in an agile way. We'll have a project's section that will list the projects and access their settings, but so simple. And then we'll have a Sprints view where user will review the tikects status (see SprintBoardView and components for more info)

Everything must be simplified for this view, we must create sections clean and simple, users using it has no tech skills, and more important, no time.

@Mockups create mockups for the project and sprints components, mockups must be functional so we can see if we are missing important things

Rethinking done. Here's what I'm delivering — two standalone, runnable mockups that share the approved visual language, but with **plain-language, no-jargon** structures.

**Screen 1 — `solopreneur-projects.html`**
- **Projects list**: one card per project (name, plain status pill `Live / In progress / Paused`, what it is in one sentence, % done, tasks, last update). A "needs your OK" banner, filter chips (All / Live / In progress / Needs you) and the topbar search filtering live.
- **Project detail** with 3 tabs: **Overview** (what this is · waiting for you · recent activity), **Sprints** (current sprint progress → jump to board, previous sprints table), **Settings** (4 plain settings + "Pause this project" with confirm).
- **Add new project** modal (3 fields, inline validation).

**Screen 2 — `solopreneur-sprints.html`**
- Sprint header: project breadcrumb, sprint name, dates, days left, big progress bar, 4 stats (Done / In progress / To do / Needs you), sprint selector.
- Board with **only 3 columns** (To do · In progress · Done), ticket cards with a one-tap **Approve** button when something waits on you.
- Ticket **drawer**: plain description, "What we need from you" box (Approve / Ask a question), status segmented control, comments + composer.
- Filter chips (All / Needs you / To do / In progress / Done), search, "Ask for something" modal creating a new ticket.

**Mock API contract**

| Method | Path | Returns |
|---|---|---|
| GET | `/api/projects` | `{ projects[] }` |
| GET | `/api/projects/:id` | `{ project }` |
| PATCH | `/api/projects/:id` | `{ project }` |
| POST | `/api/projects` | `{ projects[], project }` |
| POST | `/api/projects/:id/needs/:needId/approve` | `{ project }` |
| GET | `/api/sprints` | `{ sprints[] }` |
| PATCH | `/api/tickets/:id` | `{ ticket }` |
| POST | `/api/tickets/:id/approve` | `{ ticket }` |
| POST | `/api/tickets/:id/comments` | `{ ticket }` |
| POST | `/api/tickets` | `{ ticket }` |

**What's mocked:** latency (~170ms, 1200ms in slow mode), forced 500, empty dataset, all seed data, plus `localStorage` persistence per screen and a reset in the `mock` dev panel.

**Try it:** filter by *Needs you* → open a project → approve the waiting item → Settings → toggle a switch → Pause project. Then: open Sprints → tap **Approve** on a card → open a ticket and move it to *Done* → post a comment → reload (state persists).

**Run note:** open either file directly in a browser — no server needed.

